ow about what I'm talking  about or not but I haven't seen those  two letters but if I came out with a  newsletter it would say own the whole  market asset allocation location  rebalance that would be issued number  one issue number two would be C issue  number one it would make such a boring  newsletter that even I wouldn't  subscribe thank you  so many of the pension plans nowadays  are where you invest in subcategories  and so how does one go about picking  these subcategories based on their  expense ratio with the no in fact there  are a lot of hidden fees that you don't  even see are these pension plans are  these 401 K defined contribution plans  they they're the employer funds that you  get your funds 401 K s 40 3ds 457 s it's  really an ugly part of the industry an  ugly part of an ugly industry lots of  especially small companies offer 401 KS  and the company gets it for practically  nothing and the reason why the company  gets it for practically nothing is the  funds within the 401 K are all  outrageously expensive funds so you know  they're what I do for clients is to help  them pick the least bad and let them  know when they leave that employer or if  you no longer with that employer you can  roll it over into an IRA account and  have control to find these lower costs  funds like the ones and how a  second-grader beats Wall Street so you  know I always tell people never ever  miss out on the employer match that's  free money and now employer matches are  becoming less common beyond that you  might want to consider some other  strategies such as if you qualify tax  wise to put the additional contributions  beyond the employer match into an IRA  account some I've seen are just so  outrageously expensive don't want the  client to put any money in there above  the employer match  and there are by the way many good  usually large companies tend to have  very good 401k or 403b the  not-for-profit equivalent plans and it's  the small employer that tends to have